## CDW Introduces New Capabilities to Help Organizations Realize Value from AI Investments


November 18, 2026


*Unveiled at its 2026 Partner Summit:*


- **CDW AI Control Plane** , a new capability designed to help organizations evaluate, deploy, govern and optimize AI workloads across models, platforms and environments.
- **CDW AI Elevate** , a suite of AI services designed to help midmarket organizations accelerate AI adoption by combining business analysis and AI expertise with Forward Deployed Engineering (FDE) teams that help move AI initiatives from concept to production.
- **BuildIQ™** , an AI-native software development platform that helps organizations accelerate application delivery through a governed, AI-assisted development lifecycle.


LAS VEGAS--(BUSINESS WIRE)--


CDW (Nasdaq: CDW), the strategic end-to-end technology partner that turns customer ambition into outcomes, today announced new capabilities designed to help organizations realize greater value from their technology investments and accelerate business and mission outcomes.


Unveiled at CDW’s Partner Summit 2026, **CDW AI Control Plane** helps organizations evaluate, deploy, govern and optimize AI workloads across models, platforms and environments; **CDW AI Elevate** provides embedded engineering expertise to help customers move AI initiatives from concept to production; and **BuildIQ™** accelerates software development through a governed, AI-assisted delivery process.


As organizations navigate an increasingly complex technology landscape, many are shifting their focus from experimentation to business outcomes. However, over 40% of agentic AI projects will be canceled by the end of 2027, due to escalating costs, unclear business value or inadequate risk controls, according to Gartner, Inc.\[1\] To help customers close that gap, CDW is introducing new capabilities focused on three critical success factors: making smarter AI decisions, accelerating execution and modernizing software delivery.


"Technology creates possibility. Expertise and execution turn it into value,” said Mukesh Kumar, executive vice president and chief services and solutions officer at CDW. “By combining CDW's engineering expertise with the best of our partner ecosystem, we're helping customers choose where AI runs, understand what it costs and focus on the value it creates. For our partners, that means stronger adoption, lasting customer relationships and new opportunities to scale successful outcomes."


**Turning Technology Investments into Business Outcomes with CDW AI Control Plane**


As AI adoption grows, organizations face increasingly complex decisions around model selection, governance, infrastructure and cost management. Many are trying to determine which models to use, where workloads should run and how to operate AI securely and economically at scale.


To help customers navigate these challenges, CDW is introducing CDW AI Control Plane, a new capability currently being piloted with a select group of customers, designed to help organizations evaluate, deploy, govern and optimize AI workloads across models, platforms and environments.


At the core of the capability is CDW's proprietary decision framework, which combines benchmarking expertise, implementation experience and knowledge gained across thousands of customer engagements to help organizations match the right model to the right workload. By turning that expertise into a repeatable methodology, CDW AI Control Plane helps customers make more informed decisions about AI investments and realize business impact sooner.


As the offering evolves, it will expand to include an integrated control plane that brings together capabilities such as model routing, governance and FinOps-driven cost management into a unified experience, helping organizations operate AI more efficiently and provide visibility into what models and workloads actually cost. Combined with CDW's services and delivery expertise, CDW AI Control Plane gives customers flexibility in where AI runs, access to the expertise needed to operate it effectively and the ability to rapidly deploy workloads using infrastructure aligned to their needs. The result is reduced complexity, faster time-to-value and greater focus on business outcomes.


**Accelerating AI Deployment with CDW AI Elevate**


While access to AI technologies continues to grow, many organizations, particularly in the midmarket, lack the specialized engineering resources needed to move AI initiatives from pilot to production. AI engineers and data scientists are among the most in-demand technology roles, underscoring the challenge organizations face in securing the expertise required to scale AI successfully.\[2\] As a result, promising AI projects often stall before they can deliver meaningful business value.


To help address that challenge, CDW is introducing **CDW AI Elevate** , a service that extends CDW's Forward Deployed Engineering (FDE) model to help organizations accelerate AI adoption across cloud and frontier platforms and move from experimentation to production. Designed with the midmarket in mind, AI Elevate brings specialized engineering expertise directly to customer teams without requiring organizations to build large internal AI teams or compete for scarce talent.


AI Elevate begins with a blueprint that helps organizations understand how work moves across the business, where AI can create the most impact and which opportunities should be prioritized. Forward Deployed Engineering teams then work alongside customer teams to execute that roadmap within their workflows, with success measured by outcomes achieved in production.


By extending its FDE model to the midmarket, CDW helps organizations access the expertise, guidance and execution capabilities typically associated with much larger enterprises, shortening the path from concept to production and helping customers realize greater value from their AI investments.


**Accelerating Software Delivery with BuildIQ**


As organizations increasingly look to embed AI into business processes, the ability to move from business requirements to production-ready applications has become a competitive advantage. CDW also highlighted BuildIQ, its AI-native software delivery platform designed to help organizations move from business requirements to production-ready software through a governed, AI-assisted delivery process. Originally developed and deployed within CDW, the capability is now being used by CDW engineers to help customers accelerate software delivery.


Unlike approaches focused solely on AI-generated code, BuildIQ connects requirements, architecture, development, validation, security review and release readiness in a structured workflow produced by CDW engineers. The result is a more repeatable approach to software development with governance, traceability and deployment readiness built into the process from the start.


Together, **CDW AI Control Plane** , **CDW AI Elevate, BuildIQ,** and CDW's broader partner ecosystem help organizations address some of the most common barriers to moving AI from experimentation to production and from technology investment to business value.


These new capabilities were unveiled at CDW's annual Partner Summit, where technology partners, solutions leaders and industry experts come together to explore how innovation, services and partnerships can help organizations turn technology investments into business outcomes.


**About CDW**


CDW Corporation (Nasdaq: CDW) is the strategic end-to-end technology partner that cuts through complexity to turn customer ambition into outcomes. Working with organizations across the business, government, education and healthcare sectors in the United States, the United Kingdom and Canada, CDW enables organizations to navigate an increasingly complex technology market and turn their technology investments into lasting value. For more information about CDW, please visit CDW.com.


